/elasticsearch/issues/140018#issuecomment-3696145046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/140018","id":3696145046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAAe_f87cTrKW","user":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTgyODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5058284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner","html_url":"https://github.com/DaveCTurner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-29T10:46:51Z","updated_at":"2025-12-29T10:46:51Z","body":"> Alternatively, we could generalize `ShardBlobsToDelete` slightly\n\nOn reflection I prefer this idea. Today we work out which index metadata blobs to delete based on the difference between the two successive `RepositoryData` instances but if a blob delete fails for some reason then it won't be picked up by a future cleanup. We should instead compare the index metadata in the new `RepositoryData` instance against a listing of the index metadata blobs which really exist in the repository, since that will include any leaked blobs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/3696145046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":